Usage: soak [flags]

Run a max-rate soak load against the library or a real relay proxy.

Flags:
      --target="library"          library | relay
      --endpoint="semaphore-eval"
                                  relay endpoint: semaphore-eval |
                                  semaphore-allflags | ofrep-eval | ofrep-bulk
      --protocol="http1"          relay client and server protocol: http1
                                  (keep-alive) | h2c (HTTP/2 cleartext)
      --exporter="discard"        discard | slow | failing
      --flag="rule-bool-track"    flag key to evaluate (tracking on by default)
      --cpuprofile=STRING         write a CPU profile of the whole run to this
                                  file
      --duration=60s              total run time
      --interval=5s               sampling interval
      --flush-ms=100              exporter flush interval (ms)
      --max-events=10000          exporter MaxEventInMemory (a small backlog
                                  keeps the heap measuring leaks, not the
                                  pending events)
      --heap-tolerance=0.25       relative HeapInuse growth tolerated
      --workers=INT               number of load goroutines (default GOMAXPROCS)
      --warmup=0                  warm-up samples ignored by the verdict
                                  (default max(2, 20%))
  -h, --help                      Print this help and exit
